# cuts/v1.0.46/cut.env -- the pins this cut is made from.
#
# WHY v1.0.46 EXISTS: v1.0.45 shipped a daemon that could not contain the thing
# the cut was for. hub-v0.4.64 was built from oa c4c5b40b408e -- the SAME commit
# v1.0.45 pinned -- and published at 05:30:04Z, while the cost panel (oa #346)
# merged at 10:56:11Z. Measured with `git merge-base --is-ancestor` rather than
# read off a board row: oa #340 and #341 ARE in 0.4.64 (the nav-crop fix and
# advanced-settings genuinely shipped); #345, #346 and #347 are NOT.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🔴 DAEMON_COMMIT NAMES THE ARTEFACT, NOT THE TREE. DO NOT "UPDATE" IT.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# hub-v0.4.65 was built, Developer ID signed, notarised, stapled and PUBLISHED
# from ostler-assistant 4d1f47ae. That is a fact about a binary that exists on a
# release, and it did not change when oa main moved.
#
# So if a later reader finds oa main ahead of the pin, the correct response is
# NOT to advance this line -- it is to ask whether the daemon must be REBUILT.
# The artefact is the fact; the tree is the claim; when they disagree, change
# the claim. Editing this line to match a tree is how a cut acquires false
# provenance, which is the v1.0.14 failure.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🔴🔴 SUPERSESSION: THIS LINE WAS MOVED ONCE, AND LEGITIMATELY.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# It first read 4d1f47ae (hub-v0.4.65). It now reads 509c8333 (hub-v0.4.66).
# That is NOT the edit the rule above forbids. The forbidden edit advances the
# pin to chase a MOVED TREE while the artefact stays put. Here the ARTEFACT was
# rebuilt, so the fact itself moved and the claim follows the fact.
#
# What forced it: at 15:17:04Z, WHILE CM051 was being re-pinned to v0.4.65, oa
# PR #348 merged and oa main went 4d1f47ae -> 509c8333. verify_cut_freshness.sh
# went RED with `daemon 4d1f47ae -> 509c8333 STALE:+1`. #348 touches
# web/src/lib/i18n.ts, web/src/pages/Cost.tsx and Cost.coverage.test.ts.
# web/ IS BAKED INTO THE HUB APP, so no hold could be evidenced -> REBUILD.
# 🔴 THE RULE: any path that reaches the artefact forces a rebuild. The
# directory list (crates/, src/) is a HINT, NOT THE TEST. Control for the
# predicate: the same measurement over a known code commit returns 6 paths.
#
# ROOT CAUSE of the mid-cut move, from Andy directly rather than inferred from
# git: Archie2 merged #348 acting on a stale predicate Andy had given him,
# logged under `andygmassey` because that is the CREDENTIAL. Two consequences
# worth carrying: (1) GIT ATTRIBUTION UNDER A SHARED CREDENTIAL IDENTIFIES A
# KEY, NOT A PERSON -- ask a human, never infer an actor from `committer=`;
# (2) the fix is FRESHNESS AT THE POINT OF ACTION, not a lock. oa main was
# re-read immediately before publishing and confirmed still at 509c8333.
# The freeze note (HR015/launch/FREEZE_oa_main_v1046.md) is a CONVENTION, NOT
# A CONTROL -- measured: 0 of 71 open oa PRs had auto-merge armed, with a
# control proving the probe fires.
#
# oa PR #349 (the hub-app build-info emitter) is DELIBERATELY NOT MERGED before
# this cut. It was still unmerged at the rebuild (verified NOT tracked at
# 509c8333 -- it is present only as untracked tooling in the build checkout), so
# the daemon row is FRESH rather than HELD, and the emitter that produced the
# hub-app sidecar is a LOCAL script, not a shipped one.
# Discriminator run before deciding, not assumed: does anything in
# the v1.0.46 pipeline consume the emitter FROM THE TREE, e.g. a gate that
# re-derives the sidecar instead of reading the published one?
#   CM051 origin/main  grep -l 'emit-build-info|emit-hub-build-info' -> 0 files
#   OS003 origin/main  same predicate                                -> 0 files
#   CONTROL, same repos, 'build-info'                -> 18 and 5 files
# So the predicate is live and the zero is real absence. Both consumers I read
# (scripts/verify_cut_freshness.sh, scripts/verify_cut_manifest.py) FETCH the
# published release asset over the API. Nothing re-derives. #349 lands after
# the tag, in v1.0.47.
#
# ARTEFACTS, verified against the SERVER rather than against what was uploaded
# (daemon re-downloaded from the release and re-hashed):
#   ostler-releases   hub-v0.4.66  ostler-assistant-...-v0.4.66.tar.gz  431eeceb
#                     TeamIdentifier=V95N2B8X7A, source=Notarized Developer ID,
#                     stapler rc=0
#                     CONTROL: a de-signed copy of the same binary -> spctl rc=3
#   ostler-assistant  hub-v0.4.66  ostler-hub-app-...-v0.4.66.tar.gz    777fab12
#                     Signature=adhoc, TeamIdentifier=not set -- CORRECT, adhoc
#                     BY DESIGN, the DMG carries the outer seal
#                     CONTROL: stapler rc=65 "does not have a ticket stapled",
#                     against the daemon's rc=0 on the same command
# Both build-info.json files report 509c8333, and for the Hub app that value was
# PROBED out of the Mach-O inside the shipped tarball, not copied from a build
# log (HR015 #225/#732).
#
# 🔴 ONE ARTEFACT PER REPO IS STRUCTURAL, NOT TIDINESS. build-macos.yml fires on
# a tag push in oa and attaches its OWN unsigned daemon tarball to the
# ostler-assistant release under the same name but different bytes (measured on
# v0.4.65: 10,259,874 by github-actions[bot] vs the signed 10,151,143 in
# ostler-releases). verify_cut_freshness.sh selects assets by
# endswith(".sha256"), so two same-suffixed assets on one release is an
# ambiguity, not a cosmetic issue. install.sh defaults to ostler-releases, which
# is why the customer path stayed correct.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CM051
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CM051 names the tree whose install.sh SHIPS, compared by BLOB IDENTITY and not
# by ancestry. 67112249 is main immediately after CM051 #1048 merged -- the
# re-pin to hub-v0.4.66. The PR that updates this file touches cuts/ ONLY -- not
# install.sh, not gui/Makefile -- so the blob it names is the blob that ships.
#
# 🔴 THAT IS THE WHOLE REASON THERE ARE TWO PRs. Bundling the re-pin and this
# file into one commit would leave CM051= naming a tree whose install.sh no
# longer exists on main, and the cut could build the OLD install.sh still
# carrying the 0.4.65 pin. A pin and the WITNESS to that pin cannot ride the
# same commit.
#
# 🔴 A DAEMON BUMP TOUCHES FOUR PIN SITES, AND TWO OF THEM ARE DIGESTS.
# Verified on origin/main AFTER the merge, not from the PR diff:
#   gui/Makefile  DAEMON_VERSION      0.4.66
#   gui/Makefile  DAEMON_SHA256       431eeceb...  (the ostler-releases copy)
#   gui/Makefile  HUB_APP_SHA256      777fab12...  (the ostler-assistant copy)
#   install.sh    OSTLER_ASSISTANT_VERSION          0.4.66
#   install.sh    DEFAULT_ASSISTANT_TARBALL_SHA256  431eeceb...
# The first pass moved only the two VERSION sites, because the sweep was keyed
# on the string "0.4.64" and a SHA-256 does not contain its version number. A
# search that cannot express the thing it is looking for returns a confident
# partial answer. tests/test_daemon_pins_agree.sh caught it: 10 passed / 0
# failed after the fix, and locally that run is STRICTLY STRONGER than CI's,
# because on the runner site 6 reports "[skip] could not reach hub-v0.4.66 in
# ostler-assistant (auth/offline). NOT a pass" for want of an ostler-ai token.
# Sweep for the OUTGOING DIGEST as well as the outgoing version.
#
# The v0.4.66 re-pin applied that lesson: the sweep was keyed on the outgoing
# VERSION *and* both outgoing DIGESTS, and all five sites moved in one pass.
# 10 passed / 0 failed, re-run a second time AFTER the CI duplicate landed on
# the ostler-assistant release so the ambiguity was measured, not assumed.
#
# ASSISTANT_FALLBACK_VERSION stays at 0.4.62 deliberately. It is the
# last-known-good retry target, not a mirror of the pin; moving it in lockstep
# would leave a bad primary pin with nothing older to fall back to.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VENDOR ROWS: TWO GRAFTS AND AN ACK, NOT A WAVE-THROUGH
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# verify_cut_freshness.sh refused this cut at RC=1 "DO NOT CUT" on two vendor
# rows, from three HR015 commits that landed 2026-08-25 AFTER v1.0.45 was cut.
# Adjudicated per file against the SHIPPED tree, with a control proving the
# probe can see (vendor/ostler_fda/extract_all.py PRESENT):
#   #694 13754987  identifier_quality.py    VENDORED -> GRAFTED
#   #698 975a8de8  apple_mail_mbox.py       VENDORED -> GRAFTED
#   #695 accbc425  test_whatsapp_pair.py    ABSENT   -> hold_ack
# Pins HELD, not advanced: advancing ostler_fda means regenerating its
# divergence patch, and regenerate_forbidden_reason records that the export
# carries real person-name tokens out of a private repo into a public one.
# Gate re-run after: RC=0, stale/RED=0, fresh=17 held=5 exempt=5 cannot-verify=0.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🔴 THIS CUT HAS NO WALK RECORD AT THE MOMENT IT IS MADE.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Board #844: a green cut repoints ostler.ai/install.dmg automatically, and all
# twelve box-walk probes SKIP. Nothing between "gates green" and "customer
# download" is a runtime proof. Recording that here so the next reader does not
# mistake a green gate set for a walked build.
#
# 🔴 OFFLINE STAPLING IS NOT PROVEN AND BELONGS IN THE BOX WALK. `stapler` said
# "Downloaded ticket has been stored at..." -- that is a ticket RESOLVED OVER
# THE NETWORK, not proof of a locally stapled one. Board #221 was exactly this:
# Ostler.app shipped without its ticket and broke offline first-run. Walk test:
# pull the network, launch, watch Gatekeeper. Nobody may claim "offline install
# unaffected" until that has been done.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🔴 CM051 RE-POINTED 2026-08-26 09:35Z: 67112249 -> c32b6736
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This is the SECOND kind of legitimate move, and it is the one the file's own
# DAEMON_COMMIT rule does NOT cover. That rule forbids advancing a pin to chase
# a moved tree while the ARTEFACT stays put. Here there is no artefact yet: the
# tag has not been pushed, so nothing has been built from either value. What
# moved is install.sh itself, which is exactly what this field names.
#
# WHY IT MOVED: six PRs merged 01:07-01:10Z closing the v1.0.45 BRICK -- the
# installer's Python wrote .pyc into the notarised app on first import, broke
# the code seal, and macOS said "damaged and can't be opened" to every customer.
# Three of the six touch install.sh:
#     90f34998  #1051  PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX in install.sh, not only in the GUI
#     c0a6c194  #1054  guard the other three python LaunchAgents
#     0061df9a  #1056  CI gate: refuse a LaunchAgent with no bytecode redirect
#
# MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED. verify_cut_pin_is_current.sh at c32b6736:
#     --self-test        12 passed / 0 failed  (instrument proved live first,
#                        including its RED control and its GREEN control)
#     --cut v1.0.46      rc=1  STALE PIN
#                        install.sh @pin b26dd791 / @ref 85da4c4a
#                        and it named those same three commits
#
# 🔴 THE POINT: cutting v1.0.46 from 67112249 would have shipped the EXACT
# BRICK v1.0.46 EXISTS TO FIX. That is the v1.0.31 shape the gate was written
# for, reproduced here on the real thing rather than on a fixture.
#
# THIS PR TOUCHES cuts/ ONLY, per the two-PR rule above -- so after it merges,
# main's install.sh blob is STILL 85da4c4a, and the pin names the blob that
# ships. The gate compares BLOBS, not commits (self-test 6), so naming
# c32b6736 stays correct across this merge commit.
#
# 🔴 ORDERING CONSTRAINT THIS CREATES, AND IT IS BINDING UNTIL THE TAG:
# NOTHING MAY TOUCH install.sh BETWEEN THIS MERGE AND THE TAG PUSH. #1055 (the
# interpreter relocation, the ROOT fix) touches install.sh and is therefore
# HELD until v1.0.47 -- see the note below. Re-run the gate immediately before
# tagging anyway: a pin chosen early and trusted is a pin that goes stale while
# you are not looking, and that sentence is in this file because it already
# happened.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY #1055 IS NOT IN THIS CUT, RECORDED SO IT READS AS A DECISION
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CM051 #1055 relocates the interpreter OUT of the notarised app, which kills
# this defect class rather than guarding four entry points against it. It is
# CLEAN and it is the better fix. It is held anyway, for a reason its own PR
# body supplies: its arms were run "on a mounted artefact and a scratch HOME,
# never a real install", and it asks for a box walk. There is no box to walk
# until this DMG exists. Tagging first is therefore not a compromise -- it is
# the only order in which #1055 can get the proof it asks for. It also does not
# make #1051/#1053/#1054 redundant (its own words: defence in depth, and they
# cover boxes that installed before it lands), so holding it costs no coverage.
CUT_VERSION=1.0.48
DAEMON_COMMIT=f1c7c57d
CM051=dfebec7b9206f7f7f09029543f83e716e80cd9e9

